<html>
<title>How do I install Elf/Os 3.0 on a COSMAC Elf 2000?</title>
<body>

<h1>How do I install Elf/Os 3.0 on a COSMAC Elf 2000?</h1>

<p>
Elf/Os is a disk-based operating system for Elf-class computers designed by Mike Riley. See the <a href="http://www.elf-emulation.com">Elf/1802 Emulation</a> website.
</p>

<p>
To install Elf/Os follow these steps:
</p>

<h2>1. Start the COSMAC Elf 2000</h2>

<p>
Start an Elf 2000 using ROM <tt>Elf2Kv110.bin</tt> (or later) and a VT simulator (serial or UART).
</p>

<p>
The Elf/Os loader must first be transferred into RAM using the HEX loader.
</p>

<p><strong>Command:</strong></p>

<pre>
Select HEX mode (instead of XMODEM)
Select file <tt>elfos_ram.hex</tt> via the HEX button
Unselect Auto
Press Play
</pre>

<p><strong>Result:</strong> The HEX file is transferred to memory and the Elf/Os loader becomes available.</p>

<p><strong>Command:</strong></p>

<pre>
Press Return
Type run 3000
</pre>

<p><strong>Result:</strong> The baud rate is configured and the Elf/Os installation menu appears.</p>

<h2>2. Install Elf/Os</h2>

<p>
Execute installation steps 1 to 5 from the Elf/Os installation menu.
</p>

<p><strong>Result:</strong> Elf/Os is installed on the disk.</p>

<h2>3. Install the supplement file</h2>

<p><strong>Command:</strong></p>

<pre>
Reset the Elf 2000
Select file <tt>supplement.hex</tt> via the HEX button
Press Play
</pre>

<p><strong>Result:</strong> The supplement file is transferred.</p>

<p><strong>Command:</strong></p>

<pre>
Press Return
Type run 3000
</pre>

<p><strong>Result:</strong> The installation program starts again.</p>

<p>
Execute step 4 to install <tt>xrb.bin</tt>.
</p>

<h2>4. Boot Elf/Os</h2>

<p><strong>Command:</strong></p>

<pre>
boot
</pre>

<p>
or
</p>

<pre>
b
</pre>

<p>
Both commands start the Elf/Os boot procedure. The <tt>b</tt> command is simply a short form of <tt>boot</tt>.
</p>

<p><strong>Result:</strong> Elf/Os loads from disk and the operating system starts.</p>

<h2>Using Elf/Os with Intel 8275 Video</h2>

<p>
The Intel 8275 is a programmable CRT controller used in the Elf 2000 video system to generate a character-based display.
</p>

<p>
When using Elf/Os in combination with Intel 8275 video some utilities will not work correctly because the 8275 video hardware uses part of the same memory space that is used by certain Elf/Os programs.
</p>

<p><strong>Important:</strong> It is recommended to perform the Elf/Os installation using a serial or UART configuration.</p>

<h3>LOAD command</h3>

<p>
The standard Elf/Os <tt>LOAD</tt> command cannot be used when Intel 8275 video is enabled because the command uses memory that overlaps with the 8275 video RAM.
</p>

<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>

<ul>
<li>A modified version of the <tt>LOAD</tt> command is provided.</li>
<li>This version is located at address <tt>7400-74AE</tt>.</li>
<li>The program is included in file <tt>LOAD-8275.hex</tt>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>MINIMON @ command</h3>

<p>
The <tt>@</tt> command in <tt>MINIMON</tt> will not work correctly when Intel 8275 video is enabled. The original version uses register <tt>R0</tt> as the program counter, which conflicts with the requirements of the Intel 8275 video configuration.
</p>

<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p>

<ul>
<li>A modified version of <tt>MINIMON</tt> is provided.</li>
<li>This version uses register <tt>R3</tt> as program counter.</li>
<li>The program is included in file <tt>MINIMON-8275.hex</tt>.</li>
</ul>

</body>
</html>
